  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bhanwar Lal vs State (2025:Rj-Jd:32441) on 23 July, 2025 Author: Manoj Kumar Garg Bench: Manoj Kumar Garg [2025:Rj-Jd:32441] High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan At Jodhpur S.B. Criminal Revision Petition No. 1298/2007 Bhanwar Lal S/o Banshi Dhar R/o Chak 22 Ntr, Tehsil Nohar, District Hanumangarh. ----Petitioner Versus State of Rajasthan ----Respondent For Petitioner(s) : Mr. R.K. Bohra For Respondent(s) : Mr. Vikram Singh Rajpurohit, Pp Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Manoj Kumar Garg Judgment 23/07/2025 1.",
    "facts": "Upon suspicion, the food inspector collected 750 ml. milk from the petitioner for testing on payment of Rs.10/- to the petitioner. Thereafter, at the same time, a notice on form No.6 was given to the petitioner regarding sample collection of milk. After following due procedure, the sample was tested and the same was found to be adulterated. Upon which, a complaint was presented against the petitioner after obtaining prosecution sanction. Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/152012132/ 1 3. The Learned Magistrate framed charge against the petitioner for the offence under Section 7/16 & Rule 50 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act and upon denial of guilt by him, commenced the trial. During the course of trial, the prosecution in order to prove the offence, examined four witnesses and exhibited various documents. The accused, upon being confronted with the prosecution allegations, in his statement under Section 313 Cr.P.C., denied the allegations and claimed to be innocent. In defence, two witnesses were examined. Aggrieved by the judgment of conviction, he preferred an appeal, which was partly allowed by the learned appellate court vide judgment dated 16.11.2007. Hence, this revision petition is filed before this court.",
    "arguments": "4. After arguing the case on merits to some extent, learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that he will not assail [2025:RJ-JD:32441] (3 of 5) [CRLR-1298/2007] conviction of the petitioner and confines his arguments to the alternative prayer of reduction of the sentence awarded by the trial court. He submits that the incident in the present case pertains to the year 2000. The petitioner was not having any criminal antecedents and it was the first criminal case registered against him. No adverse remark has been passed over his conduct except the impugned judgment. The petitioner has already suffered agony of protracted trial of 25 years. The petitioner has remained in custody for a period of about 22 days out of total sentence of six months' S.I. With these submissions, learned counsel prays that by taking a lenient view, the sentence awarded to the petitioner may be reduced to the period already undergone.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. After arguing the case on merits to some extent, learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that he will not assail [2025:RJ-JD:32441] (3 of 5) [CRLR-1298/2007] conviction of the petitioner and confines his arguments to the alternative prayer of reduction of the sentence awarded by the trial court. He submits that the incident in the present case pertains to the year 2000. The petitioner was not having any criminal antecedents and it was the first criminal case registered against him. No adverse remark has been passed over his conduct except the impugned judgment. The petitioner has already suffered agony of protracted trial of 25 years. The petitioner has remained in custody for a period of about 22 days out of total sentence of six months' S.I. With these submissions, learned counsel prays that by taking a lenient view, the sentence awarded to the petitioner may be reduced to the period already undergone.",
